# hitSlop template roadmap

Single-purpose digital objects worth building as `.slop` packages. The list is
ordered by product value, breadth of everyday use, and how well each template
helps establish the hitSlop design language.

- `[x]` implemented, reviewed, and ready in `examples/slops/`
- `[ ]` planned or implemented but still awaiting the current quality review
- **Paper** favors editorial hierarchy, direct editing, and clean static export.
- **Instrument** favors compact controls, inset readouts, and durable state.
- **Skin** uses a recognizable object or silhouette when it strengthens the job.

Content and visual archetypes are intentionally independent. A canonical
template can gain skins later—such as `invoice x thermal receipt` or
`habit tracker x Tamagotchi`—without becoming a duplicate template.

## Canonical template folder

`examples/slops/` is the single source folder for every maintained,
in-progress, and completed authored template. The exact inventory below is
retained as prior art, not as parallel template homes. Unlisted local archive
or prototype directories stay ignored.

- [x] Inventory each repository template and map it to one canonical slug in `examples/slops/`, consolidating overlapping versions instead of copying duplicates.
- [ ] Migrate selected archived templates into current authored packages under `examples/slops/`; repair manifests, storage, accessibility, responsive behavior, export state, and visuals as part of each migration. The archived sources now have canonical folders on the v1 document API (Xbox excluded), and every manifest under `examples/slops/` is listed in `bundled.json`. Each still needs the quality pass in this line before its box above is treated as reviewed.
- [x] Move `archive/prototypes/ambient-mixer` to `examples/slops/ambient-sound-mixer` when its P0 build begins. The canonical folder is `examples/slops/ambient-sound-mixer`.
- [ ] Retire repository-local archived and prototype source copies after their canonical replacement is verified.

## Current examples

- [x] **Invoice** — Business / Paper — Edit parties, line items, tax, payment state, and notes, then export a control-free document. **Visual:** flat warm editorial paper, confident invoice typography, crisp rules, and a restrained green signal. The icon is a cream document with a folded corner on deep green, its total the heaviest slab. Archived `archive/templates/invoice-minimal` is superseded by this version.
- [ ] **Pomodoro — quality review required** — Productivity / Instrument — Run focus and rest cycles while retaining local session state. **Visual:** a playful tomato kitchen timer with a leafy top, bold dial, compact controls, and a ripe red Finder icon. **Review:** confirm accessible focus and reduced motion, responsive sizing, and clean static capture before marking it ready.
- [x] **Kanban Board** — Work / Instrument — Name the board, add, reorder, and retire lanes, nominate a completed lane, and move work orders across lanes with live work-in-progress limits. **Visual:** anodized job-shop schedule board with an editable brushed nameplate, milled lane slots that scroll horizontally, slotted paper tickets with punched holes, an amber WIP signal, and filed grey tickets in the completed lane. The icon is three milled slots on the graphite chassis, the middle one lit amber.
- [x] **Random Picker** — Utility / Instrument — Maintain a set of choices, draw a result, and keep lightweight history. **Visual:** animated capsule utility with one prominent action.
- [x] **Alien Radio** — Music / Skin — Control a tiny media player built around a playful receiver object. **Visual:** dark alien-green radio skin with hardware-like controls.

`examples/slops/svelte-counter` is a framework fixture, not a product template,
so it is intentionally excluded from the implemented count.

## P0 — Next foundation set

- [x] **Resume** — Personal / Paper — Directly edit and reorder a polished one-page resume, including experience, education, skills, and contact details. **Visual:** flat warm ivory editorial sheet with a quiet rail, readable typography, fine rules, and one teal signal. **Prior art:** legacy Swift `Resume` template.
- [ ] **Quick Checklist — quality review required** — Productivity / Instrument — Add, reorder, complete, archive, and clear short tasks with fast keyboard entry and canonical JSON persistence. **Visual:** blush handheld utility with tactile checkboxes and a chunky completion control. **Prior art:** consolidate `archive/templates/field-notes`, `archive/templates/sqlite-field-notes`, and `archive/templates/notebook` rather than reviving overlapping note apps.
- [ ] **Weekly Planner** — Planning / Paper — Arrange appointments and tasks across a week and mark items complete. **Visual:** ruled cream desk planner with restrained red and blue markings. **Reference:** `archive/templates/weekly-planner`.
- [x] **Recipe Card** — Food / Paper + Instrument — Edit servings, ingredients, steps, a meal photo, and guided per-step timers. **Visual:** a flat dark countertop recipe with generous food imagery, warm serif type, and a focused orange cooking signal. **Reference:** `archive/templates/recipe-card`.
- [x] **Harada Method** — Planning / Paper + Instrument — Fill in the Open Window 64 chart: one core goal, eight themes, and sixty-four concrete actions that tick off individually. Editing a theme beside the goal rewrites the centre of its own block, and the reverse, so the sheet stays consistent from either direction. **Visual:** cool-white plate floating on a flat grey field, ruled in two weights only — hairlines inside each 3×3 block, heavy ink rules between them — with shaded theme centres and an indigo goal block at the heart of the grid, under a grotesk masthead. The icon is one 3×3 window in miniature: white cells on an ink plate, the centre indigo. Narrow windows collapse to one 3×3 at a time; an export is always the whole chart. Scope is the chart only, not the long-term goal form, routine sheet, or diary.
- [x] **Habit Tracker** — Health / Instrument — Track several habits, daily check-ins, streaks, and recent consistency. **Visual:** cheerful yellow Tamagotchi-style pocket board with circular check-ins. **Reference:** `archive/templates/habit-heatmap`.
- [x] **Trip Itinerary** — Travel / Paper — Organize days, stops, bookings, times, and practical notes. **Visual:** lilac transit board crossed with a boarding pass. **Reference:** `archive/templates/trip-planner`.
- [x] **Meeting Notes** — Work / Paper — Capture agenda items, freeform notes, decisions, and assigned actions in one document. **Visual:** sober green meeting memo with acid-paper accents. The icon is a green memo sheet with top clip, header rule, checklist, and acid callout card. **Reference:** `archive/templates/meeting-notes`.
- [x] **Personal Budget** — Money / Instrument + Paper — Track income, spending groups, limits, and remaining amounts for a month. **Visual:** graphite pocket calculator fused with a clean paper ledger. The icon is a dark pocket calculator body with mint green LCD screen, orange operation key, and ledger bars. **Prior art:** legacy Swift budget and financial tracker templates.
- [x] **Pocket Spreadsheet** — Money / Instrument + Paper — Fast tabular modeling with formulas (=SUM, =AVG, arithmetic), multi-cell selection stats, and CSV export. **Visual:** vintage green-bar accounting ledger housed in a dark slate chassis with formula fx bar and emerald selection box. The icon is a dark chassis with green-bar grid, active selection cell, and fx =SUM formula bar.
- [x] **Contact Card** — Personal / Paper + Skin — Edit identity, avatar, contact details, links, location, and a short introduction. **Visual:** translucent mint pager crossed with a compact Rolodex card. The icon is a frosted mint rounded badge with circular avatar aperture and contact rule bars. **Prior art:** legacy Swift `ContactCRM` template.
- [ ] **Subscription Tracker — quality review required** — Money / Paper — Track recurring costs, renewal dates, billing periods, and paused services with one document-wide currency preference and canonical JSON persistence. **Visual:** calm off-white ledger with green renewal signals and tabular totals. **Reference:** `archive/templates/subscription-tracker`.
- [x] **Ambient Sound Mixer** — Music / Instrument — Mix, mute, solo, and save volume presets for a small set of ambient channels with synthesized audio. **Visual:** smoked-glass hi-fi mixer with physical faders and green LED level bars. The icon is a dark rackmount audio mixer with 5 vertical faders and glowing LED bars. **Reference:** `archive/prototypes/ambient-mixer`.
- [x] **Countdown & Milestones** — Planning / Instrument — Count down to a target date and track intermediate checkpoints. **Visual:** compact digital departure display housed in a capsule body. The icon is a dark titanium capsule bezel with glowing amber 7-segment digital counter and milestone progress track. **Reference:** `archive/templates/countdown-milestones`.
- [x] **Slide Deck** — Pitch / Stage + Studio — Single-file presentation suite inspired by Bento with structured slide archetypes (Title, Split, Metric, Quote, Cards), live inline canvas editing, and fullscreen presenter mode. **Visual:** dark studio projector chassis housing a 16:9 widescreen canvas with Swiss red typography and orange active dot. The icon is a dark projector shell with 16:9 screen, header tag pill, split columns, and orange play badge. **Reference:** `_docs/bento-main`.

## P1 — Everyday documents and utilities

- [x] **Daily Planner** — Planning / Paper — Schedule a day, time-block important work, and keep the top three priorities in view. Draw blocks by dragging down the rail, move and stretch them by their handles, colour them by kind, and tick off the top three. **Visual:** folded appointment book on warm cream stock with a printed fold crease, a serif weekday masthead, numbered rank seals that strike through when checked, and a ruled 6am–midnight hour rail carrying four inks — navy focus, ochre meetings, green breaks, violet personal — that pack into side-by-side columns when they overlap and fade once their hour has passed, under a bright vermilion marker tracking the current time. The icon inverts the sheet — a navy plate of pale blocks cut by a vermilion NOW lozenge that overhangs onto the cream. **Prior art:** legacy Swift `DailyPlanner` template.
- [x] **Expense Log** — Money / Paper + Instrument — Rapidly record purchases and inspect category and monthly totals. **Visual:** thermal-receipt roll with crisp numeric typography and tiny category marks. **Reference:** `archive/templates/expense-pulse`.
